THOUGHT: The NullAway warning is because miscEntities.get(renderType) can be null. Other usages (e.g., line 1964) already check for null, so the safest, minimal change is to handle the null case here by returning an empty collection when there is no map for the given renderType. I’ll update the method accordingly and then run the build to confirm the error count drops by one without new errors.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '1102,1104c\  public Collection<IEntity> getEntities(final RenderType renderType) {
    Map<Integer, IEntity> entitiesByType = this.miscEntities.get(renderType);
    if (entitiesByType == null) {
      return Collections.emptySet();
    }

    return Collections.unmodifiableCollection(entitiesByType.values());
  }' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/environment/Environment.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
